@section Installation
@ifset html
<A NAME="Installation"> </A>
@end ifset

@cindex Scheme
The JACAL program is written in the Algorithmic Language @dfn{Scheme}.
So you must have or install a Scheme implementation in order to run
it.  JACAL also requires the SLIB Portable Scheme library which is
available from @uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/slib}.  The
installation procedures given here provide the SCM Scheme
implementation along with SLIB and JACAL.  If your system has a Scheme
(or Guile) implementation installed, then the @samp{scm} steps are
unnecessary.

@deftp System Unix
@deftpx System GNU/Linux

If you lack permission to install into /usr/local/, you can install
into your home directory by changing @code{/usr/local/} to your home
directory in this script.

@example
wget https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/scm/scm-5f5.tar.gz
wget https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/slib/slib-3c2.tar.gz
wget https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/jacal/jacal-2a1.tar.gz
tar -xzf scm-5f5.tar.gz
tar -xzf slib-3c2.tar.gz
tar -xzf jacal-2a1.tar.gz
(cd slib-3c2; ./configure --prefix=/usr/local/; make install)
(cd scm-5f5; ./configure --prefix=/usr/local/; make scm; make install)
(cd jacal-2a1; ./configure --prefix=/usr/local/; make install)
# rm scm-5f5.tar.gz slib-3c2.tar.gz jacal-2a1.tar.gz
@end example

The command @samp{jacal} will start an interactive session.
@end deftp

@deftp System x86_64 GNU/Linux with Redhat Package Manager (rpm)
@example
wget http://groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/ftpdir/scm/scm-5f5-1.x86_64.rpm
wget http://groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/ftpdir/scm/slib-3c2-1.noarch.rpm
wget http://groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/ftpdir/scm/jacal-2a1-1.noarch.rpm
rpm -U scm-5f5-1.x86_64.rpm slib-3c2-1.noarch.rpm jacal-2a1-1.noarch.rpm
# rm scm-5f5-1.x86_64.rpm slib-3c2-1.noarch.rpm jacal-2a1-1.noarch.rpm
@end example

The command @samp{jacal} will start an interactive session using ELK,
Gambit, Gauche, Guile, Larceny, MIT-Scheme, MzScheme, Scheme48, SCM,
or SISC.  Type @samp{jacal --help} for instructions.
@end deftp

@c @deftp System Apple
@c @uref{http://www.io.com/~cobblers/scm/} has downloads and utilities for
@c installing SCM and SLIB on Macintosh computers.
@c @end deftp

@deftp System x86 Microsoft
Download and run
@uref{http://groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/ftpdir/scm/slib-3c2-1.exe},@*
@uref{http://groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/ftpdir/scm/scm-5f4-1.exe}, and@*
@uref{http://groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/ftpdir/scm/jacal-2a1-1.exe}.
@end deftp


